  "cSays": {
    "openPoints": [
      {
        "question": "Does the sanction of inadmissibility in form in article 15 attach to each of the six listed elements, including element 6 (supporting documents) which applies only 'where appropriate'?",
        "readings": [
          "Yes: every listed element is under the sanction, and element 6 only when there are documents to cite.",
          "Element 6 is not sanctioned because it is conditional; only elements 1 to 5 are."
        ]
      },
      {
        "question": "Does a petition missing signature, date, lodging at the registry or the right number of copies (article 14) cost inadmissibility?",
        "readings": [
          "No: article 14 states no sanction and these items are not in the article 15 list.",
          "Yes: they are conditions of the written petition, so article 15's sanction reaches them by implication."
        ]
      },
      {
        "question": "Is article 15 element 4 (legal person: name, nature, seat, representative's capacity) mandatory only when a party is a legal person?",
        "readings": [
          "Yes, only for a legal-person party.",
          "It is a general element in all petitions."
        ]
      },
      {
        "question": "Does the 20-day period in article 16 paragraph 3 run on the summons or on the petition, and how is it counted?",
        "readings": [
          "It runs from delivery of the summons to the first hearing date, as written; counting rules are not stated in the texts given.",
          "It is a condition on the whole filing and affects the petition."
        ]
      },
      {
        "question": "Is the mandatory conciliation attempt in divorce (article 439) a prior step before filing or a step inside the proceedings, and what happens if it is skipped?",
        "readings": [
          "It is a step inside the proceedings after filing, within 3 months of filing; no sanction is stated.",
          "It is a precondition to the judge's ruling on the merits."
        ]
      },
      {
        "question": "Which cases are excused from payment of fees before registration under article 17 paragraph 1, and which publication rules make a right 'published' under article 17 paragraph 3?",
        "readings": [
          "The texts given do not say; the fee and land-registry laws are needed.",
          "The petition is exempt where legal aid or a statutory exemption exists (not in the texts given)."
        ]
      },
      {
        "question": "What do 'existing or potential interest' and 'standing' cover in article 13?",
        "readings": [
          "Standing is the plaintiff's own personal quality as holder of the right; interest is the benefit sought.",
          "Both are assessed by the judge as the facts show; the texts give no definition."
        ]
      },
      {
        "question": "The slots on formal notice, non-conciliation records, limitation, forfeiture, administrative grievances, payment orders and the specialised commercial court are not settled by any text given here.",
        "readings": [
          "They belong to other modules.",
          "These texts offer no rule to test them for the petition formal elements."
        ]
      }
    ],
